# Build context for the backend image (docker-compose.local.yml -> context: ./quorumtrading-backend,
# dockerfile: quorumtrading-bootstrap/src/main/docker/Dockerfile.jvm).
#
# That Dockerfile starts with `COPY . .`, so without this file EVERYTHING here is shipped to the
# Docker daemon and baked into the build stage — including `.env`, which is gitignored precisely
# because it holds real broker credentials. The final image is multi-stage and only keeps
# target/quarkus-app, so secrets never reached a distributable layer, but they did sit in the local
# build cache, and a single-stage Dockerfile or a `docker save` of the build stage would have
# published them. Keep secrets out of the context in the first place.
#
# Everything the build actually needs stays: the root pom, every module's pom + src, and the Maven
# wrapper. The image runs `mvn` from the maven base image, and compiles from source — it never
# reads a prebuilt target/.

# Secrets. The reason this file exists.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local build output — 256 MB of it, and stale by definition: the image rebuilds from source.
# Shipping it also risks a host-built artifact shadowing the one produced in the container.
target/
*/target/
**/target/

# Local tooling and editor noise
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Never needed at build time
**/.git
**/.gitignore
README.md
